 $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287696 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287697 13194139534428 true] [17592186287696 1089 "q-10061" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287696 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534428 true] [17592186287696 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287696 1113 #uuid "a813812e-454b-50d8-be77-8c4858095748" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287696 1145 "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287698 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287699 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287700 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287701 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287702 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534428 true] [17592186287697 1041 "selection" 13194139534428 true] [175921862