 [17592186287776 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287777 13194139534428 true] [17592186287776 1089 "q-350887" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287776 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534428 true] [17592186287776 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287776 1113 #uuid "d4245d1b-ea43-5712-83b8-544965e9daa0" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287776 1145 "If we let $u={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287778 13194139534428 true] [17592186287777 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534428 true] [17592186287777 1041 "field-1" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287777 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287778 13194139534428 true] [17592186287777 1110 #uuid "e2770ca5-0f64-5e6b-9d33-6c7afcd06ce6" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287778 1034 "\\ln(4)-\\ln(3)" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534428 true] [17592186287778 1111 #uuid "e0892abf-f18d-50b0-9400-19b799bfd082" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287779 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287780 13194139534428 true] [17592186287779 1089 "q-350901" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287779 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534428 true] [17592186287779 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287779 1113 #uuid "31265c46-0cc2-5457-8780-81ed14552e3e" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287779 1145 "If we let $u=8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5)=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nSo, differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $6$ | $5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\cdot 24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{6}^{5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287781 13194139534428 true] [17592186287780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287782 13194139534428 true] [17592186287780 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534428 true] [17592186287780 1041 "field-1" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287780 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287781 13194139534428 true] [17592186287780 1110 #uuid "3d40771b-259f-5872-819b-9d0b3486f7ae" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287781 1034 "\\ln(6)-\\ln(5)" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534428 true] [17592186287781 1111 #uuid "27306d91-64bd-55c1-ac13-b345eeea365d" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287782 1034 "0" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534428 true] [17592186287782 1111 #uuid "2fd95e72-5037-5f2b-aef4-5dd99ac7150b" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287783 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287784 13194139534428 true] [17592186287783 1089 "q-350904" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287783 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534428 true] [17592186287783 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287783 1113 #uuid "7392953b-370c-5ac1-9356-c75a7236a22c" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287783 1145 "If we let $u=2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x),$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{4}^{3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534428 true] [17592186287784 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287785 13194139534428 true] [17592186287784 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287786 13194139534428 true] [17592186287